# Using similarity-ts for Synapse Code Quality and Refactoring

When working with the Synapse project during the REFACTOR phase of TiDD workflow, use `similarity-ts` to identify code duplication, maintain pattern consistency, and ensure architectural compliance across the TypeScript codebase.

## Core similarity-ts Commands for Synapse

### Basic Project Analysis
```bash
# Full project similarity analysis
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 5 src/

# Focus on specific areas with better threshold
similarity-ts --threshold 0.75 --min-lines 3 src/commands/
```

### TypeScript-Specific Analysis
```bash
# Enable experimental type similarity checking
similarity-ts --experimental-types --threshold 0.85 src/

# Include type literals and interfaces
similarity-ts --include-types --include-type-literals --threshold 0.8 src/

# Focus only on interfaces for service layer consistency
similarity-ts --interfaces-only --threshold 0.9 src/services/interfaces/
```

## TiDD Workflow Integration

### REFACTOR Phase - Code Duplication Detection
The primary use case for similarity-ts in Synapse's TiDD workflow:

```bash
# Comprehensive refactoring analysis
similarity-ts --threshold 0.75 --min-lines 4 --print src/

# Focus on pure functions
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 3 --filter-function create src/commands/
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 3 --filter-function validate src/commands/

# Service layer duplication detection
similarity-ts --threshold 0.85 --min-lines 5 src/services/implementations/
```

### GREEN Phase - Pattern Validation
Ensure new implementations follow established patterns:

```bash
# Validate new command follows existing patterns
similarity-ts --threshold 0.7 --min-lines 3 src/commands/ticket/

# Check service implementation consistency
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 4 src/services/implementations/
```

### SQUASH Phase - Final Consistency Check
Before integration, ensure codebase consistency:

```bash
# Final consistency validation
similarity-ts --threshold 0.7 --min-lines 3 --no-size-penalty src/

# Type system consistency
similarity-ts --experimental-types --threshold 0.9 src/common/types.ts src/services/interfaces/
```

## Synapse Architecture-Specific Analysis

### Pure Function Pattern Consistency
```bash
# Check command function similarity (should be low - each command is unique)
similarity-ts --threshold 0.6 --min-lines 5 --filter-function-body "CLIResult" src/commands/

# Validate pure function signatures
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 2 --filter-function-body "args.*services" src/commands/

# Check error handling patterns (should be similar)
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 3 --filter-function-body "ValidationError" src/commands/
```

### Service Layer Analysis
```bash
# Interface consistency checking
similarity-ts --interfaces-only --threshold 0.8 src/services/interfaces/

# Implementation pattern consistency
similarity-ts --threshold 0.7 --min-lines 5 src/services/implementations/

# Cross-service pattern analysis
similarity-ts --threshold 0.6 --min-lines 4 --filter-function-body "async.*Promise" src/services/
```

### CLI Command Pattern Validation
```bash
# Command structure consistency
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 4 --filter-function-body "Command" src/commands/

# Action handler patterns
similarity-ts --threshold 0.7 --min-lines 3 --filter-function-body "action.*async" src/commands/

# Error handling consistency in CLI
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 3 --filter-function-body "console.error" src/commands/
```

### TypeScript Interface and Type Analysis
```bash
# Type definition consistency
similarity-ts --experimental-types --include-types --threshold 0.9 src/common/types.ts

# Interface implementation consistency
similarity-ts --interfaces-only --allow-cross-kind --threshold 0.8 src/services/interfaces/

# Type literal similarity in function signatures
similarity-ts --include-type-literals --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 2 src/
```

## Advanced Refactoring Patterns

### Identifying Refactoring Opportunities
```bash
# Find high-similarity functions that should be extracted
similarity-ts --threshold 0.85 --min-lines 6 --print src/commands/

# Detect utility function candidates
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 3 --filter-function-body "trim\|validate\|format" src/

# Find similar error handling that could be centralized
similarity-ts --threshold 0.9 --min-lines 4 --filter-function-body "catch.*error" src/
```

### Cross-Module Consistency
```bash
# Check consistency between different command modules
similarity-ts --threshold 0.6 --min-lines 4 src/commands/ticket/ src/commands/tdd/

# Validate service layer consistency across implementations
similarity-ts --threshold 0.7 --min-lines 5 src/services/implementations/

# Common utilities identification
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 3 src/common/ src/commands/ src/services/
```

### Performance and Quality Analysis
```bash
# Identify performance-critical similar code
similarity-ts --threshold 0.7 --min-lines 5 --filter-function-body "performance\|time\|async" src/

# Find similar test patterns that could be abstracted
similarity-ts --threshold 0.8 --min-lines 4 tests/unit/ tests/integration/

# Memory usage patterns
similarity-ts --threshold 0.7 --min-lines 3 --filter-function-body "Buffer\|stream\|large" src/
```

## Threshold Guidelines for Synapse

### Recommended Thresholds by Use Case
- **Pure Functions**: 0.6-0.7 (should be unique, low similarity expected)
- **Service Implementations**: 0.7-0.8 (moderate similarity for consistent patterns)
- **Error Handling**: 0.8-0.9 (high similarity desired for consistency)
- **Type Definitions**: 0.9+ (very high similarity for type consistency)
- **CLI Commands**: 0.7-0.8 (similar structure, different logic)
- **Utilities**: 0.8-0.9 (high similarity may indicate extraction opportunity)

### Min-Lines Guidelines
- **Functions**: 3-5 lines (avoid trivial matches)
- **Service Methods**: 4-6 lines (meaningful business logic)
- **Error Handlers**: 2-4 lines (capture patterns)
- **Type Definitions**: 2-3 lines (even small types matter)

